    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d919">

                <pb facs="0835" n="719" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg719"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/2751.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American
                    Ambassador</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-10T14:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 10, 1912—2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Report received from our consul at Ciudad Juárez that at Casas Grandes
                    anti-Madero followers are making anti-American demonstrations, particularly
                    Mormon colonists, and demand surrender of their arms. You will bring this
                    information at once to the attention of the Mexican Government, and, making all
                    necessary reservation regarding injuries and damages, emphatically protest
                    against the taking of firearms from American citizens in Mexico, either by
                    Federals or revolutionists, on the ground that American citizens would be left
                    without means of protecting themselves from marauding robbers during the
                    prevailing widespread lawlessness. You will make an especially urgent request
                    for whatever alleviative action is possible at Casas Grandes.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
